#!/bin/sh
# Starts walt.id Wallet API 2 with this directory's configuration and the demo relying-party root as the only
# trust anchor for x509_hash and x509_san_dns clients. The root is generated by keygen, so the configuration is
# written at start.
set -eu
cd /waltid-wallet-api2
rm -f config/*.conf
cp /waltid/*.conf config/
{
  echo 'publicBaseUrl = "http://waltid-wallet:7006"'
  echo 'clientIdTrust { x509TrustAnchors = [ """'
  cat "${TRUST_ANCHOR_FILE:-/keys/verifier-root.pem}"
  echo '""" ] }'
} > config/wallet-service.conf
exec java -cp @/app/jib-classpath-file id.walt.wallet2.MainKt
